      "source": "SlowMist",
      "text": "Hacker Exploits Flaw in Decentralized Bitcoin Exchange Bisq to Steal $250K."
    },
    {
      "source": "RevertIQ",
      "text": "Bisq’s v1.2 protocol flaw allowed attackers to hijack fallback payouts during trade timeouts, resulting in thefts totaling approximately 3 BTC and 4,000 XMR (~$250,000) from seven users in April 2020. Trading was suspended and the flaw was promptly patched. Bisq v1.2 did not verify that the fallback payout address matched the DAO-set donation address when resolving deadlocked trades. Attackers could set this address, redirecting funds from timeouts directly to their own wallet."
    }
